{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["occ"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"@property","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"readonly","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NSArray<MLNPolygon *>","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:Q$objc(cs)NSArray"},{"text":" * ","kind":"text"},{"text":"interiorPolygons","kind":"identifier"},{"text":";","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The area occupied by any interior polygons is excluded from the overall shape.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Interior polygons should not overlap. An interior polygon should not have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interior polygons of its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If there are no interior polygons, the value of this property is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The array of polygons nested inside the receiver."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon\/interiorpolygons"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"interiorPolygons","externalID":"c:objc(cs)MLNPolygon(py)interiorPolygons","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"fragments":[{"text":"interiorPolygons","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"interiorPolygons","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"occ","url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/